App is the ability to use CSS modules.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ea13176882d1bc9361c692e9c45f74d3?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":10,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-08-04T01:18:00.000Z"},{"id":"eeQbBUnt1","title":"Learn React 18: Using Controlled Inputs","url":"https://code.tutsplus.com/react-fundamentals-using-controlled-inputs--cms-42011t","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/learn-react-18-using-controlled-inputs-eeqbbunt1","summary":"The primary way to get information from users is through forms. In React, form input elements can either be controlled or uncontrolled. Controlled inputs are those form elements whose value is controlled by the React component state. In this tutorial, we will learn the basics of controlled inputs in React.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7c40e793d6be431357f41876723516b6?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2023-08-03T01:17:09.000Z"},{"id":"33kfDlhrp","title":"Learn React 18: Using Uncontrolled Inputs","url":"https://code.tutsplus.com/react-fundamentals-using-uncontrolled-inputs--cms-42012t","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/learn-react-18-using-uncontrolled-inputs-33kfdlhrp","summary":"Using a controlled input, we were responsible for setting and updating the values of our form input elements. This meant that we had to create listeners for all these events to update values. We also used the attribute to set the value for each input element. With uncontrolled inputs, we don't have to worry about setting or updating input values.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/dd5d6fdc18a6d4056907cd1a709cafff?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2023-08-02T01:14:00.000Z"},{"id":"yRnRRmT3N","title":"Learn React 18: Writing Components as Classes","url":"https://code.tutsplus.com/react-fundamentals-writing-components-as-classes--cms-42010t","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/learn-react-18-writing-components-as-classes-yrnrrmt3n","summary":"A component is considered to be mounted when it is first rendered to the DOM. Mounting and unmounting are part of a component's lifecycle. There are special methods called and which run after a component is mounted and unmounted respectively. We can set up a timer here that will update the state of our component every two seconds.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/805642c9d2be4190b80436525b9bb42a?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2023-08-01T01:11:00.000Z"},{"id":"NBtdoEvfD","title":"Create a Music Player on Android: User Controls","url":"https://code.tutsplus.com/create-a-music-player-on-android-user-controls--mobile-22787t","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/create-a-music-player-on-android-user-controls-nbtdoevfd","summary":"Create a Music Player on Android: User Controls | Envato Tuts+ We are building a simple music player app for Android in this series of tutorials. So far, we have presented a list of the songs on the device and allowed the user to make selections from it, starting playback using the class in a class.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/eac20a11ff0190c9d05a79c277adb3a3?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-30T15:40:00.000Z"},{"id":"hbImnYtn1","title":"Formatting JavaScript Dates","url":"https://code.tutsplus.com/formatting-javascript-dates--cms-107619t","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/formatting-javascript-dates-hbimnytn1","summary":"JavaScript provides a built-in object that allows you to easily manipulate date and time. ISO The International Organization for Standardization offers a widely used format for representing dates and times in a human- and machine-readable format. In this tutorial, we will delve into the art of Formatting JavaScript objects into common formats.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6b2d5ccded7d6aadf4447db6ac914473?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2023-07-30T15:34:00.000Z"},{"id":"CU4JiWLRK","title":"How to Implement Drag and Drop With JavaScript","url":"https://code.tutsplus.com/implementing-javascript-to-drag-and-drop--cms-107629t","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-implement-drag-and-drop-with-javascript-cu4jiwlrk","summary":"Drag and drop is a user interface (UI) interaction that allows users to click and hold on an element, drag it to a target location, and drop it there. In this tutorial, we'll create a simple example of a list where you can reorder the items using drag and drop.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/32b4d6443e2e6858502281b250462f89?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":63,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2023-07-29T13:33:00.000Z"},{"id":"Z0LzPDmXu","title":"Histogram Equalization in Python","url":"https://code.tutsplus.com/histogram-equalization-in-python--cms-30202t","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/histogram-equalization-in-python-z0lzpdmxu","summary":"Histogram Equalization in Python is one of the methods you can use to enhance an image. In the next section, I will delve deeper into what is meant by histogram equalization and what happens to the image when applying the method, and then we'll see how we can implement the method in Python.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/656a7df5d6de2e71a6ea44d4feb146fc?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-28T13:31:00.000Z"},{"id":"GP3NaO9Wt","title":"Using Faker to Generate Filler Data for Automated Testing","url":"https://code.tutsplus.com/using-faker-to-generate-filler-data-for-automated-testing--cms-26824t","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/using-faker-to-generate-filler-data-for-automated-testing-gp3nao9wt","summary":"Faker is an open-source library created by Francois Zaninotto that generates artificial filler data for your application and testing needs. Faker can be used in a vanilla PHP application, a framework such as Yii or Laravel. In today's tutorial, I'll review the basic installation and usage of Faker.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4c02373a70151098379204d736de3423?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-28T13:28:00.000Z"},{"id":"Qv8ZMNIoN","title":"Using date-fns for Easy Date Manipulation","url":"https://code.tutsplus.com/using-date-fns-for-easy-date-manipulation--cms-107620t","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/using-date-fns-for-easy-date-manipulation-qv8zmnion","summary":"Using date-fns for Easy Date Manipulation is a common task in JavaScript. It's a lightweight utility library for parsing, formatting, and manipulating dates. In this tutorial, we will explore the basics of using date- fns and cover the most commonly used functions for working with dates.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/163914deaff51d3ce499769d74085d13?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-28T13:24:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["rubydispatch","verygoodventures","developercom","moralis","bootcampuxdesign"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","hamelhusain","tbpn","xai","hwchase17"],"similar":[{"id":"rubydispatch","handle":"rubydispatch","name":"Ruby Dispatch","is_squad":false,"x":-5.0575,"y":2.607,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":19,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/98dddcc8da9a4e4ca486f6426fd602ba","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.352162,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":6.210526,"tag_diversity":1.105263},"top_tags_preview":[["rails",18],["ruby",5],["database",4]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[1.1912,-8.75],"cadence_depth":[-8.3529,0.75],"hype_variety":[-7.2206,-6.1176],"title_style":[-7.1618,8.3824]}},{"id":"verygoodven